```java
public class NumberUtils {
    public static Integer createNumber(String str) throws IllegalArgumentException, NumberFormatException {
        if (str == null || StringUtils.isBlank(str)) {
            throw new NumberFormatException("A blank string is not a valid number");
        }  
        
        // Check for "--" prefix and return null in such cases
        if (str.startsWith("--")) {
            return null;
        }
        
        // Check for hexadecimal numbers and convert them to integers
        if (str.startsWith("0x") || str.startsWith("-0x") || str.startsWith("0X") || str.startsWith("-0X")) {
            int hexDigits = str.length() - 2; // drop 0x
            return Integer.parseInt(str.substring(2, 2 + hexDigits), 16);
        }
        
        // Convert the string to an integer and return it
        return Integer.parseInt(str);
    }
}
```
This code checks if the input string is null or blank and throws a `NumberFormatException` when it finds them. It also checks for hexadecimal numbers and converts them to integers, returning `null` for strings starting with "--". The rest of the string is converted to an integer and returned as the result.

