sentence2 = np.array([word2vec['A'], word2vec['cat'], word2vec[','], word2vec['sitting'], word2vec['on'], word2vec['the'], word2vec['mat']])
print(cosine_similarity(sentence1, sentence2))
```
This will give you a measure of how similar the two sentences are in terms of their meanings. The closer to 1 it is, the more similar they seem semantically. A value close to 0 would mean they're very dissimilar.
