In the context of code analysis, semantic similarity refers to how closely two pieces of code relate to each other in terms of their functionality and purpose. It is an important concept in software engineering for tasks such as code refactoring, understanding codebase, detecting bugs, etc.

Semantic similarity can be measured using various techniques like cosine similarity, Jaccard index, or even more complex methods like syntax trees comparison or neural networks-based semantic similarity models. 

